nths to understand what commitments they have.\n\nActually, let me think about the strategy first:\n\nWith 10 leave days, the optimal strategy is typically to sandwich weekends. For example:\n- Take Mon-Fri off (5 leave days) → you get Sat-Sun + Mon-Fri + Sat-Sun = 9 days\n- Do this twice: 5 + 5 = 10 leave days, giving you potentially 2 weeks + weekends = 16 days\n\nBut the maximum stretch would be something like:\n- Start on a weekend, take 2 full work weeks (Mon-Fri, Mon-Fri = 10 leave days), end after the second weekend\n- That gives: Sat-Sun (2) + Mon-Fri (5) + Sat-Sun (2) + Mon-Fri (5) + Sat-Sun (2) = 16 days\n\nWait, let me recount. If you take:\n- Week 1: Mon-Fri (5 leave days)\n- Week 2: Mon-Fri (5 leave days)\n\nAnd you depart on the Saturday before week 1 and return the Sunday after week 2:\n- Depart Sat July 18, return Sun Aug 2\n- That's 16 days (July 18 - Aug 2 inclusive = 16 days)\n\nActually, let me count more carefully. Let's say today is Friday July 17, 2026.\n\nThe earliest they could depart would be tomorrow, Saturday July 18, 2026.\n\nIf they take:\n- Week of July 20-24 (Mon-Fri): 5 leave days\n- Week of July 27-31 (Mon-Fri): 5 leave days\n\nTrip: Saturday July 18 - Sunday August 2 = 16 days (inclusive)\n\nLet me count: July 18,19 (weekend), 20-24 (5 weekdays), 25,26 (weekend), 27-31 (5 weekdays), Aug 1,2 (weekend) = 2+5+2+5+2 = 16 days.\n\nThat seems right. But I should also consider:\n- Public holidays that might fall during this period\n- Existing commitments on their calendar\n\nLet me first check for existing tasks with due dates. I should look at the period from mid-July through August 2026.\n\nAlso, I should consider: could they stretch it more? What if they start mid-week? For example:\n- Take Thu-Fri (2 days), then Mon-Fri (5), then Mon-Wed (3) = 10 days\n- That would span: Thu-Sun (4) + Mon-Fri (5) + Sat-Sun (2) + Mon-Wed (3) = 14 days? That's actually worse.\n\nThe optimal is always to sandwich full weeks between weekends.\n\nBut wait, there might be public holidays! In Singapore, National Day is August 9 (Sunday), with Monday August 10 as a public holiday. That's after the 2-week block though. And Hari Raya Haji might be around May/June 2026. Let me not guess on public holidays and focus on what the tools can tell me.\n\nLet me fetch their tasks and also look for any scheduled commitments. Let me get tasks with due dates for the upcoming months.\n\nLet me start by fetching tasks broadly."
